Q2 CONCLUSION SUMMARY:
1. SQLite Triggers enforce append-only at the database engine level.
2. Triggers work regardless of whether the query comes from the app or an external tool (verified with Python sqlite3).
3. An external tool with file write permissions CAN drop triggers (unless authorizers or OS read-only permissions are configured).
4. RECOMMENDATION: Defense-in-depth (Repository abstraction in application layer + SQLite Triggers in DDL).
